          ],
          "final_response": "I implemented all four services, but nothing has been compiled or run. `mvn` isn't installed in this environment, so the first real build will be yours.\n\n**What each service does**\n- **market-service:** `GET /api/quotes/{symbol}` returns the fixed prices. An unknown symbol gives 400.\n- **user-service:**\n  - `POST /api/users` creates a user with 10000.00 cash. A duplicate or blank username gives 400.\n  - Two internal endpoints sit behind the trade flow: `GET /internal/users/{id}` and `POST /internal/users/{id}/apply`.\n  - `apply` changes cash and position under a database lock. It rejects insufficient cash or position with 400 and an unknown user with 404, and leaves state unchanged on any rejection.\n- **trade-service:**\n  - Buy and sell validate the request first. They check the symbol against market-service, call `apply` on user-service, then save the trade in the trade database.\n  - `/api/users/{id}/trades` returns the history, with `type` set to `BUY` or `SELL`.\n  - `/api/users/{id}/portfolio` combines the user's cash and positions from user-service with prices from market-service. It returns `cash`, `cashBalance`, `holdings` (symbol, shares, price, marketValue) and `totalValue`.\n  - After each successful trade it publishes a message to `financial.exchange` with key `trade.completed`. It declares `trade.audit.queue`, and a publish failure is logged without failing the trade.\n- **api-gateway and discovery-server:** I left both unchanged. The gateway already routes portfolio and history to trade-service, which matches how I built them.\n\n**Uncertainties**\n- Because of the missing compiler, a typo or wiring error is possible.\n- A trade is saved only after user-service has already applied it. If the save fails, cash and position will have changed with no trade record. That follows from the no-distributed-transaction rule.\n- A request that is both invalid and for an unknown user gets 400, because validation runs first. The contract doesn't say which should win.",
